==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*10 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 1 second<sup>30f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage might be a bit too much if attempting it just after [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3, so obtaining at least one [[Void Fruit]] from [[Into the Future]] is recommended. Bringing anti-Dark Cats such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Cooldown Cat]] and [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Eastwood]] will help keep the Gory Darks at bay, and spamming attackers like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] can deal with the peons. As for meatshields, dual Wall Cats will work wonders, but if you don't have [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], bringing [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] and [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]] instead should do the trick.

